IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 8 (the penalty end): ss 84 to 88 -- composition, general penalties, saving of other laws, jurisdiction,
-- offences by bodies of persons.  (ss 78 to 83: deferred, see COVERAGE.md.)
-- These are the rules every offence section without a penalty of its own falls back on.

§ `s 84 Composition of offences`

-- src:5919 | 84.—(1) Any police officer not below the rank of sergeant specially
-- src:5920 | authorised by name in that behalf by the Minister, or any employee of
-- src:5921 | the Authority specially authorised by name in that behalf by the Chief
-- src:5923 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5924 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 120
-- src:5926 | Executive, may compound any offence under this Act or any
-- src:5927 | regulations made under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- src:5928 | compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably
-- src:5929 | suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding
-- src:5930 | $5,000.
@ref s 84(1) (src:5919-5930)
GIVEN `the sum asked of the person` IS A NUMBER
      `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant specially authorised by name by the Minister, or an employee of the Authority specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1): the offence may be compounded for this sum` MEANS
        `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence`
    AND `the officer is a police officer not below the rank of sergeant specially authorised by name by the Minister, or an employee of the Authority specially authorised by name by the Chief Executive`
    AND `the sum asked of the person` AT MOST 5000

-- src:5934 | (2) The Authority may, with the approval of the Minister, make
-- src:5935 | regulations prescribing the offences that may be compounded.
@ref s 84(2) (src:5934-5935)
GIVEN `the Authority has made regulations, with the Minister's approval, prescribing this offence as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(2): the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` MEANS
    `the Authority has made regulations, with the Minister's approval, prescribing this offence as compoundable`

§ `s 85 General penalties`

-- src:5941 | 85. Any person guilty of an offence under this Act or any
-- src:5942 | regulations made under this Act for which no penalty is expressly
-- src:5943 | provided shall, in addition to the forfeiture of any article seized, be
-- src:5944 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:5945 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both and, in
-- src:5946 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:5947 | $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:5948 | continues after conviction.
-- src:5950 | [65
@ref s 85 (src:5941-5950)
GIVEN `the penalty the offence section expressly provides, if any` IS A MAYBE `Penalty`
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`s 85: the penalty for an offence under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the penalty the offence section expressly provides, if any`
    WHEN JUST express THEN express
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Penalty` OF 10000, 36, 1000, TRUE

§ `s 86 Saving of prosecutions under other written laws`

-- src:5956 | 86.—(1) This Act does not prevent any person from being
-- src:5957 | prosecuted under any other written law for any act or omission
-- src:5958 | which constitutes an offence under this Act or any regulations made
-- src:5959 | under this Act, or from being liable under that other written law to any
-- src:5960 | punishment or penalty higher or other than that provided by this Act
-- src:5961 | or the regulations.
-- src:5963 | (2) A person must not be punished twice for the same offence.
@ref s 86(1) and (2) (src:5956-5963)
GIVEN `the act is also an offence under another written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has already been punished for the same offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 86: the person may be prosecuted under the other written law` MEANS
        `the act is also an offence under another written law`
    AND (NOT `the person has already been punished for the same offence`)

§ `s 87 Jurisdiction of Courts`

-- src:5968 | 87. A Magistrate’s Court or a District Court has jurisdiction to hear
-- src:5969 | and determine all offences under this Act and, despite anything to the
-- src:5970 | contrary in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, has power to impose
-- src:5972 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5973 | 121 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:5975 | the full penalty or punishment in respect of any offence under this
-- src:5976 | Act.
@ref s 87 (src:5968-5976)
GIVEN `the court is a Magistrate's Court or a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 87: the court may hear the offence and impose the full penalty` MEANS
    `the court is a Magistrate's Court or a District Court`

§ `s 88 Offences by bodies of persons`

-- src:5982 | 88. Where an offence under this Act or any regulations made under
-- src:5983 | this Act has been committed by a company, firm, society or other
-- src:5984 | body of persons, any person who at the time of the commission of the
-- src:5985 | offence was a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer or a
-- src:5986 | partner of the company, firm, society or other body of persons or was
-- src:5987 | purporting to act in such capacity shall be guilty of that offence and
-- src:5988 | shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly
-- src:5989 | unless he or she proves that —
-- src:5991 | (a) the offence was committed without his or her consent or
-- src:5992 | connivance; and
-- src:5994 | (b) he or she exercised all such diligence to prevent the
-- src:5995 | commission of the offence as he or she ought to have
-- src:5996 | exercised, having regard to the nature of his or her
-- src:5997 | functions in that capacity and to all the circumstances.
@ref s 88 (src:5982-5997)
GIVEN `the offence was committed by a company, firm, society or other body of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director, manager, secretary or similar officer or a partner, or purported to act as one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves the person exercised all the diligence to prevent it that the person's functions and the circumstances required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88: the officer or partner is guilty of the offence` MEANS
        `the offence was committed by a company, firm, society or other body of persons`
    AND `the person was a director, manager, secretary or similar officer or a partner, or purported to act as one`
    AND (NOT (`the person proves the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance` AND `the person proves the person exercised all the diligence to prevent it that the person's functions and the circumstances required`))
